export const body = "<div class=\"source-table\"><table><tbody><tr><td><p>Two months before the release, the PlayStation team finally announced the price and date for their PS5. They also confirmed their launch line-up along with their planned releases for the first year. the Xbox team has also announced their release date and price for Series X and Series S for a couple of weeks. Meanwhile the company behind the Switch seems to be sticking with the Switch for at least the next year. With all that said, we now have a pretty clear picture of what next-gen has to offer in the first year.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/cookies-inline/34e63d7a9331424b2f6b.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/cookies-inline/34e63d7a9331424b2f6b.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"647\" style=\"--source-width:313px\" alt=\"Illustration 1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/cookies-inline/79875762c95de0e3780c.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/cookies-inline/79875762c95de0e3780c.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"647\" style=\"--source-width:254px\" alt=\"Illustration 2\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/cookies-inline/121a15685e901bbe1a1f.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/cookies-inline/121a15685e901bbe1a1f.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"647\" style=\"--source-width:254px\" alt=\"Illustration 3\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td><td><p><strong>The PlayStation team will still do what they've been doing this generation</strong></p>\n<p>In the past few years, the PlayStation team has been acquiring studios and making exclusive deals to boost their first-party outputs, and this trend is not going to change one bit for the next generation. In the showing last week, they especially highlighted <em>Demon's Souls Remake</em> and <em>Spider-Man: Miles Morales</em> with two unedited gameplay demos.</p>\n<p>The <em>Demon's Souls Remake</em> demo was a true feast for the eye, boasting immaculate lighting and top-notch textures. As the majority of the game levels take place in exiguous spaces, there will be plenty of opportunities for the developer to impress players with their attention to detail.</p>\n<p>As for <em>Mile Morales</em>, the game seems to be an expansion of the PS4 game, using the same design framework with some additional kits for the titular character. This game is particularly astonishing in the VFX area, which came at no surprise since the developer has already displayed that in <em>Ratchet and Clank: Rift Apart</em>.</p>\n<p>All in all, this is perhaps the most solid launch line-up ever for Playstation fans. The only concerning aspect is the increased $70 price tag for first-party games.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>As mentioned before, the PlayStation team has been making deals with third-party developers to provide exclusives to their systems. This trend is continued with <em>Final Fantasy XVI</em>, following the <em>Final Fantasy VII Remake </em>released earlier this year. Despite how we feel about the situation, it is totally understandable for the developer to follow this path because the PlayStation team was the one trusting them in the original <em>Final Fantasy VII </em>release. Besides, the PlayStation team also backed them up financially during their crisis after their CG animation <em>Final Fantasy: The Spirits Within</em> performed poorly at the box office. So, for non-PS gamers, they will have to wait for some time to play <em>Final Fantasy XVI</em>.</p>\n<p>The developer also teased their next <em>God of War </em>game with a promised release date of 2021. Many fans, while excited, are skeptical with this release date, considering how long it took to develop the first one and the current situation of the world. That being said, we can take their word until they say otherwise. If this sequel really comes out next year along with Horizon Forbidden West, the PlayStation team is very likely to dominate 2021.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/cookies-inline/5c5c080bd76bee5f85ec.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/cookies-inline/5c5c080bd76bee5f85ec.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"647\" style=\"--source-width:313px\" alt=\"Illustration 4\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/cookies-inline/6be51f8a6f30da254530.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/cookies-inline/6be51f8a6f30da254530.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"642\" style=\"--source-width:313px\" alt=\"Illustration 5\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/cookies-inline/fd436cf900c0dbac07aa.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/cookies-inline/fd436cf900c0dbac07aa.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"647\" style=\"--source-width:254px\" alt=\"Illustration 6\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/cookies-inline/769d552589f2ae3f428a.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/cookies-inline/769d552589f2ae3f428a.webp\" width=\"960\" height=\"640\" style=\"--source-width:254px\" alt=\"Illustration 7\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td><td><p><strong>The Xbox team is shifting toward services</strong></p>\n<p>Toward the end of the last generation, the Xbox team has progressively shown more interest in services rather than exclusives to compete with the PlayStation team. Their new focus is on the Xbox ecosystem which consists of Xbox Game Pass and Project xCloud.</p>\n<p>With Game Pass, players will have access to a humongous, ever-growing library of Xbox titles from both first-party and third-party developers. The subscription fee is only $1 for the first three months; afterwards the monthly fee will lock at $9.99, and $15 if you purchase the Ultimate edition.</p>\n<p>Project xCloud is a work-in-progress game streaming service that allows players to enjoy their Xbox library on any devices—consoles, PC, or mobile phones. Game Pass also works with xCloud, meaning you can stream hundreds of games on a phone if you can afford the monthly subscription.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>That is not to say there are no games on these systems that are worth waiting. the Xbox team's flagship franchise <em>Halo</em> will unfortunately miss the launch date due to the need for polish. However, it has already been announced that the multiplayer mode will be free to play while the campaign can be experienced on Game Pass at launch, which means a lot of people will be able to enjoy the game at a very low price.</p>\n<p>Recently, the Xbox team has also acquired a dozen of new studios to enrich their first-party library, including the gigantic publisher the publisher. With the publisher, the Xbox team now have the rights to numerous system-selling IPs: <em>The Elder Scroll, Starfield, Fallout, Doom, Wolfenstein, Dishonored, Prey, </em>and<em> The Evil Within</em>. Besides, we don't know what the publisher and their studios are cooking in the oven. The future of Xbox games is absolutely brighter now in comparison to the previous generation.</p>\n<p>At the same time, the Xbox team doesn't shy away from releasing their games on other systems as shown with <em>Ori </em>and <em>Cuphead</em>. It's apparent that the Xbox team doesn't want to funnel their community to a dedicated system like the PlayStation team. Instead, they want to maximize sales across different platforms, which proved to be a logical move since the PlayStation team is also putting their exclusives on PC.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/cookies-inline/0d42eb975a381a68cb6f.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/cookies-inline/0d42eb975a381a68cb6f.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"647\" style=\"--source-width:313px\" alt=\"Illustration 8\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/cookies-inline/03fb4336221a6e18e996.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/cookies-inline/03fb4336221a6e18e996.webp\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\" style=\"--source-width:313px\" alt=\"Illustration 9\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/cookies-inline/6f08d3675e3512722bf7.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/cookies-inline/6f08d3675e3512722bf7.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"647\" style=\"--source-width:254px\" alt=\"Illustration 10\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/cookies-inline/d6550be0b4bec6140730.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/cookies-inline/d6550be0b4bec6140730.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"647\" style=\"--source-width:254px\" alt=\"Illustration 11\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td><td><p><strong>The Switch keeps its focus</strong></p>\n<p>In the Partner Direct last week, the company behind the Switch announced a wide array of third-party titles coming to the Switch, including <em>Hades</em>, <em>Ori and the Will of the Wisps</em>, and Monster Hunter Rise. Despite being released later on the system, <em>Hades</em> and <em>Ori and the Will of the Wisps</em> are two games that benefit greatly from the Switch's portability. <em>Hades </em>with its plentiful checkpoints and short time frame for each run is extremely suitable for 10 – 15 minutes of play during lunch break. The same is for <em>Ori and the Will of the Wisps</em>. And <em>Monter Hunter Rise </em>also seems to follow that pattern, on top of being an exclusive which makes it all the more unique. All in all, the company behind the Switch still doesn't care about what the other two are doing with technology and services; they just do their thing as always.</p>\n<p>As long as they keep making Mario and Zelda games, they'll be fine. (Please release a trailer for<em> Breath of the Wild 2</em>, and make a sequel to <em>Super Mario Odyssey</em>.)</p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><strong>See you next gen </strong></p>\n<p>Although every new generation of consoles has its own flavor of excitement, this upcoming one is shaping up to be extra exciting as the big Three are doing different things, giving players a wide array of options. As you can see in this article, just in the first year, we already have many heavy hitters from every one of them unlike the 8th generation. It is safe to say the only thing we should be worried about is our wallets.</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div>";
export const images = ["assets/cookies-inline/03fb4336221a6e18e996.webp", "assets/cookies-inline/0d42eb975a381a68cb6f.webp", "assets/cookies-inline/121a15685e901bbe1a1f.webp", "assets/cookies-inline/34e63d7a9331424b2f6b.webp", "assets/cookies-inline/5c5c080bd76bee5f85ec.webp", "assets/cookies-inline/6be51f8a6f30da254530.webp", "assets/cookies-inline/6f08d3675e3512722bf7.webp", "assets/cookies-inline/769d552589f2ae3f428a.webp", "assets/cookies-inline/79875762c95de0e3780c.webp", "assets/cookies-inline/d6550be0b4bec6140730.webp", "assets/cookies-inline/fd436cf900c0dbac07aa.webp"];
